    "updated_at": "2022-07-06T19:29:39Z",
    "body": "@cupen Something is weird. What you're describing is a *command duration*, which measures how long a command took to execute. `command_timeout` is used by starship internally, and it shouldn't trigger if *you* execute a long running job, only if starship is trying to run a job which is taking too long.\r\n\r\nDo you know what command is timing out?",
